meta {
  name: Finalize Draft - Missing Items (422)
  type: http
  seq: 9
}

patch {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/orders/{{orderId}}
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAccessToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "status": "ORDER",
    "items": []
  }
}

tests {
  test("422 Unprocessable Entity", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(422);
  });
  test("rejects finalizing an item-less order", function () {
    expect(res.getBody().error.code).to.equal("ORDER_REQUIRES_ITEMS");
  });
}

docs {
  Finalizing a draft to a LIVE status (`ORDER`/`QUOTE`/`APPOINTMENT`) runs the same
  required-field validation as Create Order, on the EFFECTIVE order (this patch
  merged over the persisted draft). Here `items: []` leaves the order with no
  catalogue entries, so the server rejects it with 422 `ORDER_REQUIRES_ITEMS` and
  the status flip rolls back — the draft is left unchanged. Omitting `items`
  entirely would instead validate the draft's already-persisted items.

  A real draft with no items behaves the same via the FE "Finalize as Order"
  action, which sends `PATCH /orders/:id { status: "ORDER" }`. Home-visit drafts
  missing a phlebotomist or slot are rejected with
  `ORDER_HOME_VISIT_PHLEBOTOMIST_REQUIRED` / `ORDER_HOME_VISIT_SLOT_REQUIRED`.
  See "Update Order" docs for the full list.
}
